+# QA v10: bounded original preparation result
+
+This immutable helper observes only this Game instance's original prepareLighting result, with one native Promise.then side reaction per original call. It returns exactly the original Promise/value/receiver/args/throw; no extra await, timer, render, readiness, GPU call or product state. Projection runs once on original fulfilment before Game.start terminal, and only the tiny preparationSummary is attached once to startup raw. Existing periodic snapshots and benchmark paths are unchanged.
+
+Own data descriptors whitelist real status/times/failureStep and stages.length, max16 quality scalar rows with true qualityCount/truncation/invalid flags. No stage entry, shader/resource/user data is read or retained. Missing/invalid data stays explicitly unavailable/null. Original rejection remains original and yields no fabricated timing.
+
+The instance method is restored before terminal/stop/abort, only if it is still the owned descriptor; owner/renderer/generation/scene/engine/startup abort guards reject late evidence. Raw results, Game and Promise are not retained after projection/retirement. Diagnostic errors cannot replace the original outcome. This adds startup observation overhead and is not an FPS/GPU performance claim. Full research and leaf proof: public preparation-summary-helper evidence. Root alone builds and verifies an actual capture. Original v9/source10/native remain read-only.
